---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import Callout from '../components/Callout.astro';
import { site, incorporation } from '../config/site';

const title = 'Privacy policy';
const lead =
  'What personal information the Society collects, how it is used and protected, and the choices and rights you have.';
---

<Page title={title} eyebrow="Governance" lead={lead}>
  <p class="text-small text-muted">Last updated: to be set on publication.</p>

  <h2>1. About this policy</h2>
  <p>
    The Society for Natural Capital Accounting (&ldquo;SoNCA&rdquo;, &ldquo;the Society&rdquo;,
    &ldquo;we&rdquo;, &ldquo;us&rdquo; or &ldquo;our&rdquo;) is a not-for-profit professional
    association incorporated in the Australian Capital Territory under the <em>{incorporation.act}</em>{
      incorporation.number ? ` (Association No. ${incorporation.number})` : ''
    }.
  </p>
  <p>
    This policy explains what personal information we collect through our website at
    naturalcapitalaccounting.org and in the course of our activities, how we use and protect it, and
    the choices and rights you have. It applies to members, prospective members, event participants,
    subscribers and general visitors to our website.
  </p>
  <p>
    We respect your privacy and handle personal information in a way that is consistent with the
    Australian Privacy Principles in the <em>Privacy Act 1988</em> (Cth). As a small not-for-profit,
    some of these obligations may not currently apply to us as a matter of law, but we have chosen to
    follow them as a matter of good practice. Because the Society has members and correspondents
    internationally, we also aim to meet the expectations of comparable frameworks such as the
    European Union General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR) where they apply to you.
  </p>

  <h2>2. What information we collect</h2>
  <p>
    We only collect personal information that is reasonably necessary for our activities as a
    professional association.
  </p>

  <h3>Information you provide to us</h3>
  <p>This includes information you give us when you:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      apply for or renew membership — for example your name, email address, postal or organisational
      address, professional background, area of practice and any concession category you claim (such
      as student status);
    </li>
    <li>
      pay membership fees or event fees — payment is processed by a third-party payment provider (see
      section 5); we do not store your full card details;
    </li>
    <li>register for the annual meeting, webinars or other events;</li>
    <li>subscribe to our newsletter or mailing list; or</li>
    <li>
      contact us through a web form or by email, in which case we collect your name, email address
      and the contents of your message.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Information collected automatically</h3>
  <p>
    Like most websites, our site and its hosting and analytics providers may automatically record
    standard technical information, including your IP address, browser type, the pages you view,
    referring pages and the date and time of access. This is used to keep the site running properly
    and to understand aggregate visitor traffic. Where possible, IP addresses are anonymised.
  </p>

  <h3>Cookies</h3>
  <p>
    Our site may use small text files (&ldquo;cookies&rdquo;) stored on your device to help the site
    function and to measure aggregate usage. You can disable or delete cookies through your browser
    settings, though some parts of the site may not work as intended if you do.
  </p>
  <p>
    This site stores one item locally in your browser: your choice of light or dark theme. It is not
    sent to us and is not used to identify you.
  </p>
  <p>
    We do not seek to collect sensitive information (such as health, racial or political information)
    and ask that you do not send it to us.
  </p>

  <h2>3. How we use your information</h2>
  <p>We use personal information to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>process and administer membership, including verifying eligibility and any concession claimed;</li>
    <li>collect fees and issue receipts;</li>
    <li>provide member services and run our forum, events and the annual meeting;</li>
    <li>
      send you newsletters, notices of meetings, and information about the Society's activities (you
      can unsubscribe at any time);
    </li>
    <li>respond to your enquiries; and</li>
    <li>
      meet our governance, record-keeping and legal obligations as an incorporated association.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We will only use your information for the purpose for which it was provided, or for a directly
    related purpose you would reasonably expect, unless you consent otherwise or we are required or
    permitted by law.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Consent and choice</h2>
  <p>
    By providing information to us you consent to us handling it as described in this policy. You can
    withdraw consent or change your preferences at any time — for example by unsubscribing from a
    mailing, or by contacting us using the details in section 11. Withdrawing consent may affect our
    ability to provide membership or services to you.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Disclosure and third parties</h2>
  <p>We do not sell, rent or trade your personal information.</p>
  <p>
    We share personal information only with trusted service providers who help us operate, and only
    to the extent needed for them to perform their service. These may include providers of:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>website hosting, which stores site files and server logs;</li>
    <li>payment processing, for membership and event payments;</li>
    <li>email and mailing services, which deliver newsletters and manage subscriptions;</li>
    <li>form and contact services, which deliver messages you send us; and</li>
    <li>analytics, which provide aggregate visitor statistics.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    These providers are required to handle your information in accordance with their own obligations
    and to use it only for the services they provide to us. We may also disclose personal information
    where required or authorised by law, or to protect the rights, property or safety of the Society,
    our members or others.
  </p>

  <Callout tone="pending" title="To be completed before publication">
    <p>
      Name the specific providers used for hosting, payments, mailing, forms and analytics, so that
      this section is verifiable rather than generic.
    </p>
  </Callout>

  <h2>6. Overseas disclosure</h2>
  <p>
    Some of our service providers may store or process information on servers located outside
    Australia. Where this occurs we take reasonable steps to ensure your information is handled
    consistently with this policy. As the Society grows internationally, we will keep our
    arrangements for cross-border handling of personal information under review.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Storage, security and retention</h2>
  <p>
    We take reasonable steps to protect personal information from misuse, loss, and unauthorised
    access, modification or disclosure. We hold most information electronically through the providers
    described above.
  </p>
  <p>
    We keep personal information only for as long as it is needed for the purposes described in this
    policy, or as required for our records as an incorporated association and to meet legal
    obligations. When information is no longer needed, we take reasonable steps to destroy or
    de-identify it.
  </p>

  <h2>8. External links</h2>
  <p>
    Our website contains links to external sites that we do not operate, including partner
    organisations and technical resources such as the UN System of Environmental-Economic Accounting.
    We have no control over, and are not responsible for, the content or privacy practices of those
    sites. We encourage you to read the privacy policy of any site you visit.
  </p>

  <h2>9. Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    You may request access to the personal information we hold about you, and ask us to correct it if
    it is inaccurate, out of date or incomplete. You can also ask us to stop sending you
    communications. To make a request, contact us using the details in section 11. We will respond
    within a reasonable period. There is generally no charge for making a request, though a
    reasonable cost may apply in some cases.
  </p>
  <p>
    Depending on where you live, you may have additional rights — for example under the Australian
    Privacy Principles or, if you are in the European Union or United Kingdom, under the GDPR,
    including rights to erasure and to object to certain processing. We will honour these rights
    where they apply to you.
  </p>

  <h2>10. Complaints</h2>
  <p>
    If you have a concern about how we have handled your personal information, please
    {' '}<a href="/complaints/">contact us</a> first so we can try to resolve it. If you are not satisfied
    with our response, you may be able to lodge a complaint with the Office of the Australian
    Information Commissioner at
    {' '}<a href="https://www.oaic.gov.au" rel="noopener">oaic.gov.au</a>, or with the relevant data
    protection authority in your jurisdiction.
  </p>

  <h2>11. Contact us</h2>
  <p>
    For any questions about this policy, to update your details, or to make a request or complaint,
    please contact:
  </p>
  <p>
    The Public Officer<br />
    Society for Natural Capital Accounting<br />
    <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a><br />
    naturalcapitalaccounting.org
  </p>

  <h2>12. Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>
    We may update this policy from time to time to reflect changes in our activities or in the law.
    The current version will always be available on our website, and we will note the date it was
    last updated at the top of this page.
  </p>
</Page>
